<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rector's Palace, Dubrovnik</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">15th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rector's Palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dubrovnik">Dubrovnik</a> was the seat of the government of the Republic of Ragusa and the residence of its Rector during his month in office. The present building, combining Gothic and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> forms, was largely rebuilt after a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gunpowder">gunpowder</a> explosion and fire in 1435 and again after 1463. It housed the councils, offices and prison, and is now the Dubrovnik Museums' cultural-historical collection.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rectors-palace-dubrovnik.jpg" alt="Rector's Palace, Dubrovnik" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Américo Toledano · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Museo_Cultural_Hist%C3%B3rico_de_Dubrovnik_-_Exterior_-_001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
